---
import BaseLayout from '~/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocsShell from '~/components/DocsShell.astro';
import CodeBlock from '~/components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '~/components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Python — leptris docs"
  description="pyleptris: the Python binding for libleptris via cffi (ABI mode). Parse, navigate, query with XPath 1.0, and serialize."
>
  <DocsShell
    title="Python — pyleptris"
    lede="The Python binding wraps libleptris via cffi in ABI mode: a single cdef mirroring the public headers. Parse, navigate, query, serialize — same core, same bounds."
  >
    <h2>Setup</h2>
    <p>
      <code>pyleptris</code> needs the <code>cffi</code> package and a
      <code>libleptris</code> shared library on the host. Build the library
      with the shared target (see
      <a href="/docs/getting-started">getting started</a>), then either
      install it system-wide or point <code>LEPTRIS_LIB_PATH</code> at it:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`pip install cffi
cmake -B build -S . -DLEPTRIS_BUILD_SHARED=ON
cmake --build build --target leptris_shared
export LEPTRIS_LIB_PATH=$PWD/build/src/libleptris.dylib`} />

    <h2>Quick start</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="python" code={`from pyleptris import Document

doc = Document.parse('<root><item id="1">hello</item></root>')
root = doc.root
print(root.name)                        # => "root"
print(root.first_child_element.attribute('id'))  # => "1"
print(doc.xpath('count(//item)'))       # => 1.0
doc.close()`} />

    <h2>The surface</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>Document.parse(string)</code> — the entry point.</li>
      <li><code>Document#root</code>, <code>Node#name</code> — navigation mirrors the C element surface.</li>
      <li><code>Document#xpath(expr)</code> — typed XPath 1.0 results: nodesets, booleans, numbers, strings.</li>
      <li><code>Document#serialize()</code> — output writer with indent options.</li>
      <li><code>Document#close()</code> — releases the pool; the same document-owned memory contract as every binding.</li>
    </ul>
    <Callout>
      <p>
        <strong>One cdef, one seam.</strong> The binding&rsquo;s cdef is a
        mirror of the public headers; CI&rsquo;s drift gate fails on phantom
        symbols or arity drift between the mirror and the C surface.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <h2>Where next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${SITE.githubC}/tree/main/bindings/python`}>The binding in the repo</a> — source and tests.</li>
      <li><a href="/docs/internals">Internals &amp; FFI</a> — the ABI contract the mirror implements.</li>
    </ul>
  </DocsShell>
</BaseLayout>
